SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Security Council Fails to Adopt Draft Resolution on Ending Ukraine Crisis, as Russian Federation Wields Veto","publisher":"UN Press / Meetings Coverage","publication_date":"2022-02-25","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/sc14808.doc.htm","claim":"Brazil said the Council should stop the hostilities, react to force against a member state's territorial integrity, and seek immediate suspension of hostilities through negotiation and diplomatic dialogue.","locator":"Statement by Ronaldo Costa Filho (Brazil)","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous UN meeting record with attributed Brazilian statement and vote context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in February 2022, at the start of the Ukraine war.","ruler_attribution":"Brazilian diplomacy under Bolsonaro's administration; this is not a private Bolsonaro quote, but it reflects the government's line.","contrary_evidence":["The statement is diplomatic language, not proof that Brazil could materially influence the conflict."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Despite Bolsonaro reluctance, Brazil votes against Russia on U.N. resolution","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-02-26","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/02/26/uk-ukraine-crisis-brazil","claim":"Brazil voted for the Security Council draft condemning the Russian invasion, but Bolsonaro had recently met Putin, said he was in solidarity with Russia, and later said Putin had peaceful intentions.","locator":"Lead paragraphs and lines 666-677 in the article view","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting carried by Euronews; strong independent journalism, but still secondary.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the opening week of the invasion.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Bolsonaro conduct on the Putin trip; the vote itself was a government action under his presidency.","contrary_evidence":["Brazil still voted against Russia at the UN despite Bolsonaro's remarks, so the article shows mixed rather than one-directional conduct."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.6"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"General Assembly Overwhelmingly Adopts Resolution Demanding Russian Federation Immediately End Illegal Use of Force in Ukraine, Withdraw All Troops","publisher":"UN Press / Meetings Coverage","publication_date":"2022-03-02","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/ga12407.doc.htm","claim":"Brazil voted to condemn Russia's aggression against Ukraine, demand withdrawal of Russian forces, and support an immediate peaceful resolution through dialogue, mediation, and other peaceful means.","locator":"Lead paragraph and resolution summary","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UN General Assembly record with vote totals and resolution text summary.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in March 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Brazilian government vote under Bolsonaro's presidency, not a personal Bolsonaro statement.","contrary_evidence":["The UNGA vote aligns Brazil with peace language, but it does not show Brazil had leverage to end the war."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Nota conjunta MJSP e MRE - Acolhida humanitaria de ucranianos","publisher":"Ministério da Justiça e Segurança Pública","publication_date":"2022-03-03","url":"https://www.gov.br/mj/pt-br/assuntos/noticias/nota-conjunta-mjsp-e-mre-1","claim":"Bolsonaro ordered Brazil to offer shelter to Ukrainians affected by the conflict, and the ministries issued a temporary visa and residence scheme for Ukrainian nationals and stateless people displaced by the war.","locator":"Opening paragraph of the joint note","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Brazilian government notice describing a presidentially directed policy response.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in March 2022, during the active Ukraine emergency.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to a presidential determination by Bolsonaro, though implemented through ministries.","contrary_evidence":["Humanitarian reception is positive conduct, but it does not by itself resolve the underlying war."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Governo Federal vai resgatar cerca de 70 pessoas que deixaram a Ucrânia","publisher":"Governo do Brasil","publication_date":"2022-03-08","url":"https://www.gov.br/pt-br/noticias/assistencia-social/2022/03/governo-federal-vai-resgatar-cerca-de-70-pessoas-que-deixaram-a-ucrania-1","claim":"Brazil sent a FAB KC-390 to evacuate about 70 people from the Ukraine crisis and also sent 11.6 tons of humanitarian donations for the Ukrainian population.","locator":"Lead paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government operational report on a contemporaneous repatriation and aid mission.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in March 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Government action under Bolsonaro's presidency; not personal command evidence.","contrary_evidence":["This is humanitarian support, not an independent measure of strategic peace leadership."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bolsonaro diz que nao toma partido na invasao russa da Ucrania","publisher":"UOL / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-03-30","url":"https://economia.uol.com.br/noticias/reuters/2022/03/30/bolsonaro-diz-que-nao-toma-partido-na-invasao-russa-da-ucrania.htm","claim":"Bolsonaro said he would maintain neutrality on the Russia-Ukraine war and that this was not Brazil's problem.","locator":"Lead paragraphs of the Reuters report","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting in a major Brazilian outlet; strong but secondary and the article reflects the president's own remarks.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 while the invasion was ongoing.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Bolsonaro statement.","contrary_evidence":["Brazil also voted against Russia at the UN, so Bolsonaro's neutrality line was not the whole government posture."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.6"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Brazil officially condemns the launch of an intercontinental ballistic missile by the DPRK","publisher":"Government of Brazil","publication_date":"2022-03-26","url":"https://www.gov.br/en/government-of-brazil/latest-news/2022/the-brazilian-government-has-condemned-the-launch-of-an-intercontinental-ballistic-missile-by-the-democratic-peoples-republic-of-korea","claim":"Brazil condemned North Korea's ICBM launch as destabilizing and a violation of UN Security Council resolutions, and urged adherence to the CTBT and NPT.","locator":"Lead paragraph","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official Brazilian government statement on a major international-security event.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and relevant to Brazil's lawful-security posture.","ruler_attribution":"Government statement under Bolsonaro's administration; not a direct personal Bolsonaro quote.","contrary_evidence":["This shows norm enforcement, not direct management of a live interstate conflict."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.6","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Brazil abstains on humanitarian-protection draft in the Security Council, citing lack of ceasefire language","publisher":"UN Press / Meetings Coverage","publication_date":"2022-03-07","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/sc14823.doc.htm","claim":"Brazil said a humanitarian resolution should include a cessation of hostilities, humanitarian access, and adherence to international humanitarian law, and it abstained because the draft lacked a ceasefire reference.","locator":"Statement by Ronaldo Costa Filho (Brazil)","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UN Security Council record with a detailed Brazilian explanation of vote.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in March 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Brazilian government position under Bolsonaro; not a personal Bolsonaro statement.","contrary_evidence":["The abstention shows a more cautious peace posture than a simple yes vote would have, so it cuts both ways."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Security Council Fails to Adopt Resolution Condemning Moscow's Referenda in Ukraine's Occupied Territories, as Permanent Member Employs Veto","publisher":"UN Press / Meetings Coverage","publication_date":"2022-09-30","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/sc15046.doc.htm","claim":"Brazil abstained on the resolution condemning the annexation referenda, saying the draft's scope and language did not contribute to resolving the conflict while affirming territorial integrity.","locator":"Statement by Ronaldo Costa Filho (Brazil) after the vote","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UN Security Council record with Brazil's explanation of abstention.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in September 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Brazilian government position under Bolsonaro's presidency.","contrary_evidence":["The abstention weakens the clean pro-Ukraine line seen in other Brazilian statements."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.6","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Statement by the Permanent Representative of Brazil to the United Nations, Ambassador Ronaldo Costa Filho, at the UNSC meeting on Ukraine - September 27th, 2022","publisher":"Ministério das Relações Exteriores","publication_date":"2022-09-27","url":"https://www.gov.br/mre/pt-br/delbrasonu/the-permanent-mission-of-brazil-to-the-un/the-permanent-mission-of-brazil-to-the-un/statements/2022/september-2022/statement-by-the-permanent-representative-of-brazil-to-the-united-nations-ambassador-ronaldo-costa-filho-at-the-unsc-meeting-on-ukraine-september-27th-2022","claim":"Brazil said the Ukraine referenda escalated the conflict, were not a real expression of local will under war conditions, and reiterated its call for an immediate ceasefire and peace negotiations.","locator":"Statement body on the Brazilian UN mission page","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official foreign-ministry publication of Brazil's UN statement.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in September 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Brazilian diplomatic line under Bolsonaro; not a personal Bolsonaro quote.","contrary_evidence":["Brazil's later abstention on a related resolution shows the government tried to balance territorial-integrity language with negotiation language."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"With 143 Votes in Favour, 5 Against, General Assembly Adopts Resolution Condemning Russian Federation's Annexation of Four Eastern Ukraine Regions","publisher":"UN Press / Meetings Coverage","publication_date":"2022-10-12","url":"https://press.un.org/en/2022/ga12458.doc.htm","claim":"Brazil abstained on the General Assembly resolution condemning the annexation of Ukrainian regions, and Brazil's representative said the calls for an immediate cessation of hostilities were left out of the draft.","locator":"Discussion after the vote, including Brazil's explanation","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UN General Assembly record with Brazil's explanation of abstention.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in October 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Brazilian government position under Bolsonaro's presidency.","contrary_evidence":["The same record also shows Brazil reaffirming respect for territorial integrity, so this is not a pro-Russia statement."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.6","2B.10"]}

Search and rejection summary:
I considered roughly 30 documents across these clusters: UN Security Council and General Assembly Ukraine records from February, March, September, and October 2022; Brazilian foreign ministry, justice ministry, and Casa Civil notices on Ukraine; Reuters/UOL reporting on Bolsonaro's Moscow trip and neutrality remarks; Brazilian humanitarian-reception notices; and a few out-of-scope nuclear or economic pieces that did not add direct international-conduct evidence.

Kept because they added distinct evidence:
- Brazil's direct UN voting record on Ukraine and annexation.
- Bolsonaro's own public remarks about Russia and neutrality.
- Brazilian humanitarian response toward Ukrainians.
- Brazil's explanation that ceasefire language mattered in humanitarian and annexation votes.
- A separate official condemnation of North Korea's ICBM launch as a lawful-security signal.

Rejected as duplicate, weak, or not worth repeating:
- Multiple Reuters mirrors of the same Moscow trip story once one strong Reuters/UOL version was kept.
- Generic explainer pieces about the Ukraine war that did not add Brazil-specific conduct.
- Post-2022 retrospective commentary and 2023-2024 follow-ups that did not improve attribution for 2022.
- Nuclear-safety and disarmament materials better reserved for Chapter 1B rather than 2B.
- Purely domestic Brazilian political coverage that did not bear on international peace, restraint, or lawful security.

Remaining gaps:
- Brazil had no direct interstate war or proxy campaign of its own in 2022, so 2B.2, 2B.5, 2B.8, and 2B.9 remain thin by design; more searching is unlikely to change that materially.
- The clearest ruler-level negative evidence is Bolsonaro's Russia/Putin rhetoric and neutrality line, but the record still mixes that with consistent UN and humanitarian support for Ukraine.
- If you wanted a tighter attribution layer, the next useful search would be on direct Bolsonaro remarks around the February 16 Moscow visit and any cabinet-level minutes or transcripts on Ukraine policy, but that would mostly sharpen 2B.3/2B.6 rather than change the overall exposure profile.
